[{:db/id 17592186096665 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-2450f5df-4d67-52ba-8389-fdbd1502ce3f" "question-f11e7aad-252b-5e12-b641-681cfb746b6c"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186096668 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-63aa6d59-1b3d-5a26-a1f9-94507bee325e"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186096666 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-bfe0bdd7-dbe2-5dd0-8dfa-8c8cabd2a658"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-2450f5df-4d67-52ba-8389-fdbd1502ce3f" :question/id #uuid "2450f5df-4d67-52ba-8389-fdbd1502ce3f" :question/math-academy-id "q-348699" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi /2}sin\\,(\\frac{x}{6})cos\\,(\\frac{x}{6})\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "In this case, we use the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,⇒\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\n \n\nLetting $\\theta =\\frac{x}{6},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{3}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{6})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{6}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{6})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{6})\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi /2}\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{3})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{3})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{3})]{|}_{0}^{3\\pi /2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{3})\\,{|}_{0}^{3\\pi /2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)] \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}[0-1] \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-06176425-884c-5dd3-8a01-9f1d8d2b6773"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-06176425-884c-5dd3-8a01-9f1d8d2b6773" :answer-field/id #uuid "06176425-884c-5dd3-8a01-9f1d8d2b6773" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-339e926b-935f-5ee2-947e-fc63fa89e95d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-339e926b-935f-5ee2-947e-fc63fa89e95d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-339e926b-935f-5ee2-947e-fc63fa89e95d" :answer/id #uuid "339e926b-935f-5ee2-947e-fc63fa89e95d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-f11e7aad-252b-5e12-b641-681cfb746b6c" :question/id #uuid "f11e7aad-252b-5e12-b641-681cfb746b6c" :question/math-academy-id "q-114680" :question/problem "${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "In this case, we use the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,⇒\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\n \n\nLetting $\\theta =\\frac{x}{4},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{4}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})]{|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =-[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)] \\\\  & =-[0-1] \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9ceb62bb-3be2-57db-812f-e1a858ecdd5d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9ceb62bb-3be2-57db-812f-e1a858ecdd5d" :answer-field/id #uuid "9ceb62bb-3be2-57db-812f-e1a858ecdd5d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-91b53cb9-b208-5d9d-8a4b-ed0a7d3f6fb9" :answer-field/choices ["answer-846b5800-afa9-5986-857f-46a79c9e8c41" "answer-6b8e8a0c-fae0-5beb-99c7-7f6e5e2eba40" "answer-91b53cb9-b208-5d9d-8a4b-ed0a7d3f6fb9" "answer-fafd609c-1308-5476-8673-122442085a55" "answer-453ab082-2bbc-52d2-9772-336a7f8f1822"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-846b5800-afa9-5986-857f-46a79c9e8c41" :answer/id #uuid "846b5800-afa9-5986-857f-46a79c9e8c41" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6b8e8a0c-fae0-5beb-99c7-7f6e5e2eba40" :answer/id #uuid "6b8e8a0c-fae0-5beb-99c7-7f6e5e2eba40" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-91b53cb9-b208-5d9d-8a4b-ed0a7d3f6fb9" :answer/id #uuid "91b53cb9-b208-5d9d-8a4b-ed0a7d3f6fb9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fafd609c-1308-5476-8673-122442085a55" :answer/id #uuid "fafd609c-1308-5476-8673-122442085a55" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-453ab082-2bbc-52d2-9772-336a7f8f1822" :answer/id #uuid "453ab082-2bbc-52d2-9772-336a7f8f1822" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-63aa6d59-1b3d-5a26-a1f9-94507bee325e" :question/id #uuid "63aa6d59-1b3d-5a26-a1f9-94507bee325e" :question/math-academy-id "q-10558" :question/problem "$\\int (x-{sin}^{2}⁡3x+{cos}^{2}⁡3x)\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we use the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =3x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x={cos}^{2}⁡3x-{sin}^{2}⁡3x.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (x-{sin}^{2}⁡3x+{cos}^{2}⁡3x)\\text{d}x & =\\int (x+{cos}^{2}⁡3x-{sin}^{2}⁡3x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b1b91902-f580-5044-b5d2-4725b9ece1f0"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b1b91902-f580-5044-b5d2-4725b9ece1f0" :answer-field/id #uuid "b1b91902-f580-5044-b5d2-4725b9ece1f0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-fc0f2c74-19ed-5e9c-96ae-282dcffd9a14" :answer-field/choices ["answer-117955a3-da81-5764-9c65-84ef3f86d82f" "answer-a73a5c77-6d93-5e05-ae26-4069ce27113c" "answer-fc0f2c74-19ed-5e9c-96ae-282dcffd9a14" "answer-c453cd7a-bf5c-5377-a103-509b529efe7e" "answer-0f0f1116-d915-5ec7-81c7-f4086a52153e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-117955a3-da81-5764-9c65-84ef3f86d82f" :answer/id #uuid "117955a3-da81-5764-9c65-84ef3f86d82f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a73a5c77-6d93-5e05-ae26-4069ce27113c" :answer/id #uuid "a73a5c77-6d93-5e05-ae26-4069ce27113c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fc0f2c74-19ed-5e9c-96ae-282dcffd9a14" :answer/id #uuid "fc0f2c74-19ed-5e9c-96ae-282dcffd9a14" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c453cd7a-bf5c-5377-a103-509b529efe7e" :answer/id #uuid "c453cd7a-bf5c-5377-a103-509b529efe7e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0f0f1116-d915-5ec7-81c7-f4086a52153e" :answer/id #uuid "0f0f1116-d915-5ec7-81c7-f4086a52153e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186318595 :answer-field/correct "answer-878d0ada-2dc4-521b-bbd5-3ae173141b72" :answer-field/choices ["answer-878d0ada-2dc4-521b-bbd5-3ae173141b72"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-878d0ada-2dc4-521b-bbd5-3ae173141b72" :answer/id #uuid "878d0ada-2dc4-521b-bbd5-3ae173141b72" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7\\pi}{2}-\\frac{\\pi^{2}}{2}-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-bfe0bdd7-dbe2-5dd0-8dfa-8c8cabd2a658" :question/id #uuid "bfe0bdd7-dbe2-5dd0-8dfa-8c8cabd2a658" :question/math-academy-id "q-361712" :question/problem "![](images/a7/a71e9121e38cfa60bfac0864ee2686cad756e268b78b512f55367bf6af0f8c94.png)\n\nFind the area $A$ of the region in the $xy$-plane that is bounded by the curve $y=4{cos}^{2}⁡(2x)+{sin}^{2}⁡(2x),$ the $x$-axis and the lines $x=0$ and $x=\\frac{\\pi }{4},$ as shown above. Do not round the answer\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The area of the region is given by\n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}(4{cos}^{2}⁡(2x)+{sin}^{2}⁡(2x))\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nRecall  ${cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x=1,$ so we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{cos}^{2}⁡(2x)+{sin}^{2}⁡(2x) & =3{cos}^{2}⁡(2x)+({sin}^{2}⁡(2x)+{cos}^{2}⁡(2x)) \\\\  & =3{cos}^{2}⁡(2x)+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we use the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${cos}^{2}⁡x$ term, given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=2{cos}^{2}⁡x-1.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n2{cos}^{2}⁡x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1.\n$$\n\nHence, the area of the region is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}(3{cos}^{2}⁡(2x)+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}(\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+\\frac{3}{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}(\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+\\frac{5}{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{3}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+\\frac{5}{2}x)|}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =[\\frac{3}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4})+\\frac{5}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4}]-[\\frac{3}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\cdot 0)+\\frac{5}{2}\\cdot 0] \\\\  & =[\\frac{3}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )+\\frac{5\\pi }{8}]-[\\frac{3}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)+0] \\\\  & =[\\frac{3}{8}\\cdot 0+\\frac{5\\pi }{8}]-[\\frac{3}{8}\\cdot 0+0] \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\pi }{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5275b8a3-a8ed-51bd-8426-91952cbec909"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5275b8a3-a8ed-51bd-8426-91952cbec909" :answer-field/id #uuid "5275b8a3-a8ed-51bd-8426-91952cbec909" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-8c2da0af-70e4-5430-8430-baeb3a4118a8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8c2da0af-70e4-5430-8430-baeb3a4118a8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8c2da0af-70e4-5430-8430-baeb3a4118a8" :answer/id #uuid "8c2da0af-70e4-5430-8430-baeb3a4118a8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5\\pi}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186318511 :answer-field/correct "answer-1e4f061a-ff83-54a7-966d-5615c8fefe75" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1e4f061a-ff83-54a7-966d-5615c8fefe75"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1e4f061a-ff83-54a7-966d-5615c8fefe75" :answer/id #uuid "1e4f061a-ff83-54a7-966d-5615c8fefe75" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\pi" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186318549 :answer-field/correct "answer-140301e9-e5d7-5ea2-aa4c-0f869d4dbf85" :answer-field/choices ["answer-140301e9-e5d7-5ea2-aa4c-0f869d4dbf85"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-140301e9-e5d7-5ea2-aa4c-0f869d4dbf85" :answer/id #uuid "140301e9-e5d7-5ea2-aa4c-0f869d4dbf85" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2\\pi" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186097922 :tutorial/content "How can we calculate $\\displaystyle{\\int} \\sin x \\cos x \\, \\textrm{d}x?$  \n\nNotice that we have the product of sine and cosine with the same argument $(x).$ In such cases, we can use the double-angle formula for sine to solve the integral.\n\nLet's recall the double-angle formula for sine, which is\n\n$$\n\\sin {2x}=2\\sin x \\cos x.\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above formula as\n\n$$\n\\sin x \\cos x =  \\dfrac{1}{2} \\sin {2x}.\n$$\n\nPlugging this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\int \\sin x \\cos x \\, \\textrm{d}x&=\\int \\dfrac{1}{2}\\sin {2x} \\, \\textrm{d}x\\[5pt]\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t&=\\dfrac{1}{2} \\int \\sin {2x} \\, \\textrm{d}x\\[5pt]\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t&=\\dfrac{1}{2} \\left( -\\dfrac{1}{2} \\cos {2x}\\right )+C \\[5pt]\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t&=-\\dfrac{1}{4} \\cos {2x}+C.\t\n\t}\n$$\n\nIn general, we can use the double-angle formula for sine to solve any integral that's of the form \n\n$$\n\\int \\sin\\left(ax+b\\right)\\cos(ax+b)\\,\\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\n Let's take a look at another example." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186097923 :tutorial/content "Let's recall the three double-angle formulas for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x) & ={cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & =2{cos}^{2}⁡x-1 \\\\  & =1-2{sin}^{2}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can use the double-angle formulas for cosine to integrate $\\sin^2{x}$ and $\\cos^2{x}.$ Let's take a look at some examples." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186096847 :activity/expected-seconds 1380.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id 17592186097508 :step/math-academy-id 637993 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186097509 :step/math-academy-id 637994 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186097510 :step/math-academy-id 637997 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186097513 :step/math-academy-id 637998 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186097511 :step/math-academy-id 638001 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186097512 :step/math-academy-id 638004 :db/ensure [:step/validate]}]
